  "authorNotes": "Scope: lessons 18–29 of the 2026 book. The Mohammadpur 2026 final is the same book, so much of it was reusable: all 10 word meanings, 5 of 8 sentence-making words, the 4 conjuncts, 5 short questions, 2 long questions and the paragraph title. MP items from lesson 15 (কাজের আনন্দ: 'দল বেঁধে চলে', 'আহরণ', 'তৃণলতা') and the poem-based long question ('ছোট নদী সম্পর্কে চারটি বাক্য') were left out: lesson 15 is outside the syllabus and long questions must come from stories. The MP Final 2025 paper is also the same book (lessons 18+), so it was used as the second source. No Mohammadpur paper has an MCQ or punctuation section in Bangla, so those are NEW (the punctuation items are the book's own exercise on p.55). Doubts: (1) Row 3 'যুক্তবর্ণ ভেঙে শব্দ লেখ' was read as 'break the conjunct into its letters and write one word with it' — please confirm. (2) Row 5 words with the vowel signs removed have a single intended answer, but a child may find another real word; accept any correct word. (3) Row 11 item 2 (ছয় ঋতু) is a prose lesson but not a story in the narrow sense; swap for an item from 'দুখু মিয়ার জীবন' or 'নববর্ষ' if the school reads 'গল্প' strictly. (4) Duration '৩ ঘণ্টা' is copied from the MP paper; the syllabus does not give one."
